                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dcf47093-3695-3b9c-ab30-64212aaa012b",
                        "entry_id": "f163b102-a8f5-32e0-b5eb-3f2bf271ebbb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Référence au prénom ou au nom d’une personne décédée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3825326-52bd-4a14-87ad-e33bc4fd4adc",
                                "sense_id": "dcf47093-3695-3b9c-ab30-64212aaa012b",
                                "text": "Un nécronyme est une sorte de synonyme du mot homonyme qu’on utiliserait pour nommer un nouveau-né se substituant à un mort."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "284f5f35-1ce6-3327-b9db-3a00c18696ff",
                        "entry_id": "f163b102-a8f5-32e0-b5eb-3f2bf271ebbb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prénom de naissance d’une personne trans, celui de l’acte de naissance avant le choix d’un nouveau prénom."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca5d7fcb-5dae-4539-bdb9-c41a3854587f",
                                "sense_id": "284f5f35-1ce6-3327-b9db-3a00c18696ff",
                                "text": "Ma \"cheffe\" qui me nécronyme par mail dans le plus grand des calmes, en plus de systématiquement parler de moi au masculin aux collègues et étudiant•es."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f1f7bec3-4a84-4f0e-9e99-2c717f4ed515",
                        "source_entry_id": "f163b102-a8f5-32e0-b5eb-3f2bf271ebbb",
                        "target_lang_word": "deadname",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "deadname",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20ab6ecc-e662-37b3-ab73-b0ed409225d0",
                                        "entry_id": "d46fa298-ce90-35cc-85c4-719d74e756df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A previous name of a person (especially a transgender person) who has since changed their name."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "neologism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f65ef7a-35c5-40ad-9a29-8ca91fb365d5",
                                                "sense_id": "20ab6ecc-e662-37b3-ab73-b0ed409225d0",
                                                "text": "And when people constantly refer to you as your deadname [a name that you previously went by], or use the incorrect pronouns, it really is like getting slapped with a wet fish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1af51eaf-43f2-4b6f-93c6-470d43cbadde",
                                                "sense_id": "20ab6ecc-e662-37b3-ab73-b0ed409225d0",
                                                "text": "One of the articles in our last issue contained a major error: we referred to a transgender student by their deadname."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab4536c7-e8a4-4fb6-b65b-980bfa3f94f0",
                                                "sense_id": "20ab6ecc-e662-37b3-ab73-b0ed409225d0",
                                                "text": "“My deadname is everywhere because of my ID card, and not only do I have to look at it but lots of other people get to see. […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fed8350-9cf4-4a39-8a70-065131732c17",
                                                "sense_id": "20ab6ecc-e662-37b3-ab73-b0ed409225d0",
                                                "text": "I know it hurts you when they look at you strange\nMisgender you intentionally, use your deadname"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "deadname",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b190c576-a46f-39d4-aa4c-347677f5c760",
                                        "entry_id": "a6056ee0-e2e1-3351-bd5b-0c40ef597311",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To refer to someone (especially a transgender person) who has changed names by a previous name."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf1828f9-c4ef-4937-9a72-4c96cff218df",
                                                "sense_id": "b190c576-a46f-39d4-aa4c-347677f5c760",
                                                "text": "Using trans peoples' dead names – names that they were born with which are either wrong through either legal or preferential means – has been and always will be an act of aggression, not just to the person you're deadnaming but to all trans people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1569deb2-a038-4e33-84bc-ec35a1976ab5",
                                                "sense_id": "b190c576-a46f-39d4-aa4c-347677f5c760",
                                                "text": "\"Right now, it's unclear whether they are choosing to deadname me maliciously, or just can't be bothered to accommodate trans students in the way we require them to,\" he said."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54af1aab-4649-4980-8aff-75a2736e8f63",
                                                "sense_id": "b190c576-a46f-39d4-aa4c-347677f5c760",
                                                "text": "Felix's dad deadnames him despite supporting his top surgery and hormone therapy, and he hates his mom for leaving when he was 10."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
